atlas schema
# The meta-schema: what an atlas entry is. Human-facing contract; atlas.py is the
# machine enforcer. Three levels are mandatory -- never stop at a domain label:
#   DOMAIN          broad semantic territory
#   ARCHITECTURE    an independent calculus / state machine (one atlas entry)
#   INTERNAL CALCULI its actual node types, edges, transitions, invariants
#
# An architecture block accepts these keys (repeatable keys become lists):
#
#   architecture <id>
#     canonical_name       PascalCase name (required)
#     family               registry family/dir (required)
#     domain               broad semantic territory (required)
#     layer                where it sits in the stack
#     semantic_question    the one question it answers (required)
#     purpose              why it exists
#     maturity             architectural|declared|implemented|measured|proven (required)
#     node_types  ...      its own node ontology (repeat)
#     edge_types  ...      its own edge ontology (repeat)
#     state_types ...      its state machine states (repeat)
#     internal_calculus .. named sub-structures / algorithms (repeat)
#     child       ...      child architecture ids (repeat)
#     invariant   ...      laws that hold (repeat)
#     forbidden_inference  what may NOT be inferred -- the highest-value field (repeat)
#     interacts   ...      architecture ids it bridges to (repeat)
#     computational_form.. durable|fused|trajectory|coupled|... (repeat)
#     native_format ...    graf|flux|delta|crux|helix|axon|kore|fuse|bfp (repeat)
#     command     ...      public command identities that own/participate (repeat)
#     source_path ...      real implementation paths (repeat)
#     witness     ...      real tests/fixtures/receipts proving maturity (repeat)
#     source_lineage ...   originating documents/prior names (repeat)
#     historical_name ...  prior identities (repeat)
#     supersedes / superseded_by
#     known_gap   ...      honest gaps (repeat)
#     cooling_path / reheat_condition
#
# CONSTITUTIONAL RULES enforced by atlas.py validate:
#   1. maturity measured|proven REQUIRES a witness (no laundering by parent label).
#   2. a view must expand to >=2 real architectures (collapse is reversible zoom,
#      never a replacement).
#   3. an interaction must connect two real registered architectures.
#
# A view block:
#   view <ViewName>
#     expands_to <architecture-id>   (repeat; >=2)
#
# An interaction block:
#   interaction <id>
#     source <architecture-id>
#     destination <architecture-id>
#     relation <name>
#     preserves ...            semantics carried across (repeat)
#     drops ...                semantics intentionally dropped (repeat)
#     forbidden_inference ...  what the bridge must NOT promote (repeat)
#     authority ...            authority required (repeat)
#     invalidates_on ...       when the projection goes stale (repeat)
#     witness <type>
#     binding <impl path> (repeat)
